CAT = "hkle1Conduct"; SEG = "CND"
Q = [
("Which is one of the nine general principles of the SFC's Code of Conduct?",
 "Honesty and fairness", ["Lowest possible fees", "Guaranteed returns", "Majority shareholder rule"],
 "The Code's general principles are honesty and fairness, diligence, capabilities, information about clients, information for clients, conflicts of interest, compliance, client assets and responsibility of senior management."),
("Before recommending a product, a licensed person must ensure it is reasonably suitable for the client. This requirement is now:",
 "A client agreement term", ["Only a guideline for banks", "Waived for all online trades", "Applied only to large trades"],
 "Since June 2017 the client agreement must include a clause that any product solicited or recommended will be reasonably suitable, so suitability is a contractual obligation."),
("\"Know your client\" under the Code of Conduct means finding out a client's:",
 "Finances, experience, objectives", ["Political views and religion", "Employer's share price", "Favourite brokers and banks"],
 "Before dealing, a licensed person should take reasonable steps to establish the client's true identity, financial situation, investment experience and investment objectives."),
("A client opens a securities account. Under the Code of Conduct the firm must:",
 "Sign a written client agreement", ["Lend the client money", "Guarantee the first trade's profit", "Register the client with HKEX"],
 "A written client agreement setting out each side's rights and obligations, with the relevant risk disclosure statements, is required before services are provided."),
("A client wants a broker to trade without asking each time. The broker should first:",
 "Get written authority", ["Rely on the client's nod", "Trade within its own limits", "Notify HKEX of the account"],
 "A discretionary account needs the client's written authority, an explanation of what it covers, and confirmation of the authority each year."),
("A broker receives a large client buy order in a thinly traded stock and buys some for its own account first. This is:",
 "Front running", ["Best execution", "Fair allocation", "Order aggregation"],
 "Trading for one's own account ahead of a client's order, using knowledge of it, is front running and breaches the Code's client priority rule."),
("Under the Code of Conduct, when a client order and a staff member's order are on the same terms, the firm should:",
 "Fill the client's first", ["Fill the staff order first", "Split them at random", "Cancel both of the orders"],
 "Client orders must be handled fairly and in the order received, with priority over orders for the firm's own account or for staff."),
("A licensed person executes a client order on the best available terms. This duty is called:",
 "Best execution", ["Churning", "Warehousing", "Order aggregation"],
 "The Code requires best execution: taking reasonable steps to execute client orders on the best available terms, considering price, cost, speed and likelihood of execution."),
("Under the Code of Conduct, telephone recordings of client orders must be kept for at least:",
 "6 months", ["1 week", "7 years", "12 months"],
 "Where client orders are received by telephone, a recording system must be used and the recordings kept for at least 6 months."),
("A firm's employee wants to trade shares for her own account. The firm should:",
 "Have a staff dealing policy", ["Ban all staff from investing", "Let her trade through any broker", "Allow her trades only after hours"],
 "The Code requires firms to have policies on employees' own dealing, normally requiring staff accounts with the firm or with notice, and trades never ahead of clients."),
("A broker has a material interest in a product it recommends. Under the Code it should:",
 "Disclose the conflict", ["Hide it to avoid confusion", "Refuse to deal with the client", "Charge a higher fee to cover it"],
 "A licensed person should avoid conflicts and, where they cannot be avoided, disclose them and ensure fair treatment of the client."),
("Which client may be treated as an institutional professional investor without further assessment?",
 "A licensed corporation", ["A retired teacher", "A small family company", "A new university graduate"],
 "Institutional professional investors, such as licensed corporations, banks and insurers, fall within the definition in the SFO itself. Individuals and corporations need assessment under the Professional Investor Rules."),
("Before a firm treats a corporate professional investor as such for Code of Conduct exemptions, it must generally:",
 "Assess it and get consent", ["Ask the SFC's approval", "Charge a higher commission", "Close the client's other accounts"],
 "The firm assesses the corporation's knowledge, expertise and experience, explains the consequences of being treated as a professional investor and the right to withdraw, and gets its written consent. Individual professional investors no longer qualify for these exemptions."),
("When selling a complex product to a client, the Code of Conduct requires the firm to:",
 "Explain its nature and risks", ["Keep its features confidential", "Only sell it by phone", "Avoid any written warning"],
 "For complex products, firms must ensure the transaction is suitable, provide sufficient information on key nature, features and risks, and give warning statements."),
("Which conduct breaches the Code of Conduct on giving information to clients?",
 "Overstating a fund's past returns", ["Giving a risk disclosure statement", "Sending a contract note on time", "Explaining commission charges"],
 "Information for clients must be accurate and not misleading. Promotional claims about performance must be fair and balanced."),
("A firm offers clients its own research while also trading the stock for itself. Under the Code it should:",
 "Not trade ahead of the research", ["Trade ahead to save costs", "Withhold the research from clients", "Send it only to staff"],
 "Firms must not trade on research before clients have had a fair opportunity to act on it, and conflicts in research must be managed and disclosed."),
("When a client's margin account falls short, the Code of Conduct expects the firm to:",
 "Make a margin call promptly", ["Sell all positions without notice", "Lend the client more money", "Ignore it until month end"],
 "A firm should have a margin policy, call for margin promptly and act fairly and consistently, informing clients of the terms that apply to their account."),
("A client complains about a broker's handling of an order. The firm should:",
 "Investigate it and respond", ["Ignore unwritten complaints", "Close the account at once", "Pass it to HKEX to handle"],
 "The Code requires complaints to be handled timely and appropriately, investigated by staff not involved, and the client told of further avenues such as the FDRC."),
("The Fund Manager Code of Conduct (FMCC) applies mainly to persons licensed for:",
 "Type 9 asset management", ["Type 1 dealing only", "Type 10 credit ratings", "Leveraged foreign exchange"],
 "The FMCC sets out conduct standards for persons licensed or registered to manage collective investment schemes and discretionary accounts under Type 9."),
("Under the FMCC, a fund manager placing one order for several funds must:",
 "Allocate fills fairly", ["Give the best price to its own fund", "Let the broker decide", "Allocate to the largest fund only"],
 "Fund managers must allocate aggregated trades fairly and consistently among the accounts concerned, never favouring their own or a connected account."),
("Under the FMCC, a fund manager's soft dollar arrangements are acceptable only if:",
 "Clients benefit and are told", ["They pay the manager's office rent", "They are paid in cash to staff", "They are kept from clients"],
 "Goods and services received for directing business must demonstrably benefit clients, be on best execution terms and be disclosed. Cash rebates go to the client."),
("The Corporate Finance Adviser Code of Conduct applies to:",
 "Type 6 advisers", ["Licensed insurance agents", "MPF scheme trustees", "Share registrars only"],
 "The CFA Code sets standards for persons licensed or registered for Type 6 advising on corporate finance, including sponsors and financial advisers."),
("Under the CFA Code, a corporate finance adviser should not act if:",
 "Its conflicts are unmanageable", ["The client is a listed company", "The deal is very large", "Another adviser is also hired"],
 "A corporate finance adviser must manage conflicts of interest and decline to act where a conflict would impair its independence or the client's interests."),
("The Code of Conduct for Persons Providing Credit Rating Services applies to firms licensed for:",
 "Type 10", ["Type 4", "Type 8", "Type 12"],
 "Credit rating agencies and their analysts are licensed for Type 10 regulated activity and must follow the CRA Code on quality, independence and transparency."),
("A credit rating agency's analyst wants to own bonds of an issuer she rates. Under the CRA Code this is:",
 "Not allowed", ["Allowed with board approval", "Allowed if under a set value", "Allowed after the rating"],
 "Analysts must not hold securities of the rated entity, to protect the independence and objectivity of ratings."),
("Which body is subject to the SFC's Code of Conduct for Share Registrars?",
 "Listed companies' registrars", ["Stock Exchange participants", "MPF scheme trustees", "Banks' private banking units"],
 "Registrars of Hong Kong listed companies are regulated through the Code of Conduct for Share Registrars, which covers fair treatment of shareholders and safeguarding records."),
("Under the Code on Open-Ended Fund Companies, an OFC's custodian must be:",
 "Independent of the manager", ["The fund's largest investor", "A licensed corporation for Type 1", "Appointed by HKEX"],
 "The OFC Code requires the custodian to be functionally independent of the investment manager and to safeguard the OFC's scheme property."),
("A firm's staff member asks a client to sign a blank order form to save time. Under the Code this is:",
 "Improper", ["Good practice", "Required for margin accounts", "Allowed for regular clients"],
 "Firms must not have clients sign blank or incomplete documents; client agreements and instructions must be complete and accurate."),
("Under the Code of Conduct, a firm handling client assets must:",
 "Safeguard them properly", ["Pool them with its own cash", "Invest them for its own gain", "Hold them in staff accounts"],
 "General principle 8: a licensed person should promptly and properly account for and adequately safeguard client assets."),
("Under the Code of Conduct, who is ultimately responsible for a firm's compliance with proper standards?",
 "Senior management", ["Its newest staff", "The SFC's case team", "Its own clients"],
 "General principle 9 places primary responsibility on senior management for ensuring appropriate standards of conduct and adherence to proper procedures."),
]
